  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian protection for vulnerable people in Arauca and Caquet&#xe1;, Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Severe flooding from intense rains which have been compounding since May 2025 has affected 44,000+ people in Arauca and Caquet&#xe1;, Colombia as of 17 July. River overflows and isolation in Arauca, and crop and infrastructure damage in Caquet&#xe1;, have led to displacement, loss of livelihoods, and heightened protection risks&#x2014;especially for rural communities exposed to armed groups. Oxfam Colombia, with APOYAR and Corpomanigua, proposes a five -month response (Aug&#x2013;Dec 2025), targeting 2,500 people across Protection, Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WaSH), and Livelihoods. Support will include shelter kits, hygiene items, water filters, food, and psychosocial care. Priority will be on in -kind assistance (58.43%) and services (12.98%) with a gender -sensitive approach.</narrative>
  </description>
